| 4 | AT THE MERGE | the operator's carry rite by stage then swap, the merge's proof (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/the-worn-house`>>), walked by the operator's hand on 2026-11-17 off the rite card, whose restore now stands as the founding runbook's 11a (lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/carry-across-refound). BUILT: the old house (image `983c705`) censused and exported; a brand-new hearth founded at `~/.lares-next` beside the old with no pūlama (founded twice: a paste carried the first founding's cold-key card lines into the chat, so that hearth burned before anything landed), three faces minted with their own routes and paper, seeds and imports per face, parity accepted on five named rows (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/rite-heal-list), the `row-key` sweep, the keep lei strung by hand while no pūlama stood; then the swap by rename into `~/.lares`; then the lit house of rank 4a on the renamed root, the first keep pushed to the backup repo (its tessera `par`), and `lares home tend` (generation 4). The prior house rests whole at `~/.lares-prior` and its image at `lares-surface:pre-carry`, and a rollback renames back. Runbook 11a now walks the restore from a keep at one revision (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/carry-across-refound`>>). WAITING: the burn of `~/.lares-prior` and `lares-surface:pre-carry`, ruled at its default (operator, 2026-11-18, #/rulings): it burns after one keep restore drill reads par (rank 13b) and `docker ps -a --filter ancestor=lares-surface:pre-carry` reads empty, in backlog-alpha #/next; the friction the walk met heals at rank 4f | The operator ruled the carry the merge's proof, and each act in it belonged to the operator's hand on a real terminal; the rename keeps the old house readable until the operator burns it. The pūlama binds the house's paths and restarts unless stopped, so it lights after the swap, on the renamed root: lit at `~/.lares-next`, it would keep binding a path the rename empties. |

